  📗
    The built-in request logger, as middleware: 🧱 app 📝 app❗️❗️. One line
    for each request at info: the method, the path as it was sent, the status
    and how long the rest of the pipeline took.
  📗
  ❗️ 📝 ➡️ 🍇📨🍇📨➡️📬🍉➡️📬🍉 🍇
    💭 The logger, not the app: a closure that held the app would be held by it in turn.
    📢 👇❗️ ➡️ sink
    ↩️ 🍇🎍🥡 request 📨 next 🍇📨➡️📬🍉 ➡️ 📬
      ⏱🐇🔩❗️ ➡️ started
      ⁉️ next request❗️ ➡️ response
      ↪️ 👀 sink 🔤info🔤❗️ 🍇
        💭 The target as it was sent and not the decoded path, so that the line shows what the client wrote.
        ✌️🐇🧰 🥩 request❗️ 🔤?🔤❗️ ➡️ pieces
        🔤🔤 ➡️ 🖍🆕path
        ↪️ 📏 pieces❓ ▶️ 0 🍇
          🐽 pieces 0❗️ ➡️ 🖍path
        🍉
        🚦 request❗️ ➡️ method
        🔡 🚥 response❗️ 10❗️ ➡️ status
        🔡 ⏱🐇🔩❗️ ➖ started 10❗️ ➡️ took
        📝 sink 🔤info🔤 🆕🔡 🍿 method 🔤 🔤 path 🔤 🔤 status 🔤 🔤 took 🔤ms🔤 🍆 🔤🔤❗️ 🍿 🔤method🔤 method 🔤path🔤 path 🔤status🔤 status 🔤durationMs🔤 took 🍆❗️
